# Longest Strictly Increasing or Strictly Decreasing Subarray

**LeetCode Problem:** [3105. Longest Strictly Increasing or Strictly Decreasing Subarray](https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-strictly-increasing-or-strictly-decreasing-subarray/)

## Approach: Two-Pass Traversal

- Traverse the array to find the longest strictly increasing contiguous subarray.
- Maintain a counter `start`, incrementing it when the current element is greater than the previous element. Otherwise, reset it to `1`.
- Repeat the same process to find the longest strictly decreasing contiguous subarray.
- Return the maximum of both lengths.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int longestMonotonicSubarray(vector<int>& nums) {
        int maxi_1 = 0, maxi_2 = 0;
        int start = 1;

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {
            if(i > 0) {
                if(nums[i] > nums[i-1]) start++;
                else start = 1;
            }
            maxi_1 = max(maxi_1, start);
        }

        start = 1;

        for(int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {
            if(i > 0) {
                if(nums[i] < nums[i-1]) start++;
                else start = 1;
            }
            maxi_2 = max(maxi_2, start);
        }

        return max(maxi_1, maxi_2);
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(N)\) — Two traversals of the array.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(1)\) — Only a constant number of variables are used.
